==English==

===Etymology===
Coined from {{etyl|el}} [[τετρά-]] ([[tetra-]]) + [[tennis]].

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-proper-noun|-}}

# {{video games|trademarks}} A puzzle [[video game]] in which [[falling]] [[tetromino]]es must be manipulated to form complete lines.

====Quotations====
* '''2005''': Jack Leonard, ''Bad Altitude''
*: ''While I worked out a '''''Tetris'''''-like arrangement to get all of the leftovers into the oven, Phil's curiosity got the better of him.''

